  "raw": {
    "https://www.ursinus.edu/careers-and-outcomes/": {
      "title": "Careers & Outcomes",
      "description": "Careers & Outcomes | Careers and Outcomes | Ursinus College Skip to main content Visit Apply Request Info Make a Gift Search Ursinus.edu Menu Menu and Search Close Expanded Main Menu Search Ursinus.edu Search About Academics Admission APEX Life at Ursinus News & Events Careers & Outcomes Athletics Graduate Partnerships Arts at Ursinus Give to Ursinus Request Info Visit Apply Information for: Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parents Admitted Students Menu Menu and Search Careers & Outcomes You’ll find Ursinus alumni thriving at Google, Vanguard, Merck, the Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia, in courtrooms, national parks, state houses, sports medicine clinics, and even at the United Nations. They are activists, lobbyists, CEOs, educators, writers, and scientists. This breadth reflects the versatility of an Ursinus degree—and the return on investment it delivers. APEX at Ursinus allows students to have hands-on, immersive experiences, beginning their first year on campus. Top 6% for ROI Ursinus is ranked in the top 6% of all colleges and universities for return on investment. Making New Grads Rich The Wall Street Journal names Ursinus a top school nationally doing the best job at improving the financial futures of our grads. 97% Within six months of graduating, 97% of graduates are employed, attending graduate or professional school full time, completing a fellowship, or engaged in a year of service. Social Mobility Named a top performer on social mobility, U.S. News & World Report Prepared. Ready to Lead. Ursinus invests in liberal arts skills that prepare students to excel in tomorrow's economy and job paths that don't exist at this point. How they define success is ultimately up to them, but we can guarantee our graduates are strongly positioned, more motivated, highly creative and ready to lead APEX at Ursinus Career Coaches on Day One Career and Professional Development Where We Work Grad School Acceptances Shaped by the lessons he learned at Ursinus and the hours he spent in the TV studio in Ritter Hall, Shawn Witt ’01 is thriving as an executive in the entertainment industry. Meet Shawn Bindu Pirlamarla ’10 is the head of Worldwide Prime Benefits at Amazon. In this role, she leads global strategy and execution for Prime membership benefits.  As a neuroscience and business & economics double major, she gained skills at Ursinus that she applies every day at Amazon. Amazon From goalkeeper to coach, B.J. Callaghan ’03 built a career in professional soccer that started at Ursinus. He now leads Nashville SC in Major League Soccer as head coach, fresh off a 2023 CONCACAF Nations League title as head coach of the U.S. men’s national team. Meet B.J. Nashville SC Communications Katie Teuber ’09 is currently the Director, Startup Engagement for Comcast NBCUniversal LIFT Labs. She focuses on driving business development and innovation through strategic partnerships with startups. Katie served as the keynote speaker at The U-Imagine Center ’s BEAR Innovation Competition in April 2025 . Copyright 2024. All rights reserved. Aakash Shah ’10, a Rhodes Scholar and a former member of the board of trustees, was named one of 19 White House Fellows for 2021-2022. Cain Images Sherrell Dandy, Esq. ’07 is an accomplished trial attorney at the preeminent law firm, Kline & Specter and was named to the 2022 Pennsylvania Forty Under 40 selected by media news outlet, City & State Pennsylvania. Chemistry major Laura Nebel ’16 works at the intersection of chemistry and law as a patent agent at L’Oréal in NYC. In this role, Laura continually learns about the latest cutting-edge innovations and translates complex chemistry inventions into patent applications. Dan Mullen '94 has been hired as the UNLV head football coach for the 2025 season. He is a TV broadcaster covering college football for ABC and ESPN. He served as the head football coach at Mississippi State University from 2009 to 2017 and the University of Florida from 2018 until 2021. Courtesy of ESPN Former editor at Sports Illustrated Kids magazine, Ellen Cosgrove Labrecque ’95 has written over 100 non-fiction books, many of them about sports and athletes. She has authored 14 biographies in the New York Times best-selling “Who Was. . .” series, including one on Travis Kelce. Long before she was a best-selling cookbook author and host of PBS's \"Indian as Apple Pie,\" Anupy Singla '90 was just a student cooking up ideas in the kitchen of Shreiner Hall. Her Ursinus journey shows how a spark in college can grow into a career you love. © Andrew Miller, All Rights Reserved When Carolyn Smith ’11 was a student at Ursinus, it was easy to imagine her working at the United Nations like her mentor, the late U.S. Ambassador Joseph H. Melrose Jr. ’66. Today, she carries forward his legacy as an Administrative Officer at the United Nations. Karla Pisarcik '17 graduated from Villanova Law and is an Assistant District Attorney leading the High Intensity Drug Trafficking team in Montgomery County, Pa. For Kate Bormann ’18, her most recent recognition as one of the Top 30 Designers Under 30 in New York City is the culmination of the work she started as an art major and Bonner Leader at Ursinus College. Workforce vs. Graduate & Pre-Professional School Within six months of graduating, 97% of Ursinus graduates are employed, attending graduate or professional school full time, completing a fellowship, or engaged in a year of service. What is the breakdown of workforce vs. continuing education? On average, 80% of our placed-graduates enter the workforce and 20% go on to medical school, law school, to pursue a graduate degree, or MBA. Top 3 industries reported from our 2022 and 2023 are healthcare, finance, and education. By the Numbers 71.4% In 2024, Ursinus graduates had a 71.4% med school admission rate, which is roughly 28% higher than the national admission rate reported by the Association of American Medical Colleges. 100% of Ursinus students partake in an Experiential Learning Project (XLP) which requires every  student to participate in hands-on learning to gain applicable real-world experience. 97% Law School Acceptance for students who participate in the pre-law program. From Fulbright to Watson: A legacy of success Each year, Ursinus College students apply for and receive a number of prestigious, nationally competitive scholarships and fellowships. These fellowships may provide funding for portions of undergraduate study, for graduate study, or even for travel and/or independent research not tied to a degree program. Scholarships and Fellowships Pathway to careers in The Pharma Industry Ursinus College is located in a hub of innovation in biotech and pharmaceuticals. Over 800+ Ursinus alumni are actively employed in the pharma industry alone, as we continue our legacy of training the next generation of scientists. Location, location, location! The 2025 Top Employers survey from Science and the American Association for the Advancement of Science (AAAS) lists the top 20 leading companies worldwide in biotech and pharma. Thirteen of the top 20 are located within 70 miles of Ursinus College with J&J, Merck, Pfizer, GSK, Genentech, Abbvie., Quest Diagnostics and Vertex within an easy driving distance from our campus in Collegeville. @ursinuscollege Powered by Curator.io Campus Map Webmail Library Editor Login Offices and Services Employment Contact Us Berman Museum Title IX and Sex Discrimination Campus Store & Books Web Accessibility Calendars Operating Hours and Service Updates Facebook X / Twitter Instagram YouTube ©\n            2026 Ursinus College. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://www.ursinus.edu/live/profiles/11111-lecturer-position-in-microbiology-fall-2026": {
      "title": "Lecturer Position in Microbiology, Fall 2026",
      "description": "Lecturer Position in Microbiology, Fall 2026 | Human Resources | Ursinus College Skip to main content Visit Apply Request Info Make a Gift Search Ursinus.edu Menu Menu and Search Close Expanded Main Menu Search Ursinus.edu Search About Academics Admission APEX Life at Ursinus News & Events Careers & Outcomes Athletics Graduate Partnerships Arts at Ursinus Give to Ursinus Request Info Visit Apply Information for: Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parents Admitted Students Menu Menu and Search Home Human Resources Lecturer Position in Microbiology, Fall 2026 Lecturer Position in Microbiology, Fall 2026 Department Biology Overview The Biology Department at Ursinus College invites applications for an adjunct instructor to teach microbiology during the fall semester (August 24, 2026, to December 18, 2026). The position will teach a microbiology lecture (Tuesday/Thursday morning) and two sections of microbiology lab (Thursday afternoon). A minimum of a Master’s degree in the Biological Sciences/ Microbiology/Immunology or Developmental Biology, or Anatomy and Physiology, or a closely related discipline from an accredited College or University is required. Preference will be given to candidates with substantial teaching, laboratory, and curriculum development experiences Responsibilities Duties and Responsibilities: Prepare lectures and laboratory exercises Submit textbook and course syllabus Circulate course materials via Canvas learning management system Prepare and grade assignments, quizzes, exams, and lab reports Enter information in Colleague Self-Service reporting and grade submission Application Submit letter of application, CV, and graduate transcripts (unofficial transcripts are acceptable at this point in the application procedure) to here . Recommendations will be required upon interview. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the positions are filled. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement Ursinus College is a selective, independent, co-educational, residential liberal arts college of approximately 1500 students located about 25 miles northwest of center city Philadelphia. With a diverse community of students, it is an expectation of all faculty to contribute to the inclusion, engagement, and success of all students. Ursinus is an EEO employer.  Ursinus College does not discriminate on grounds of race, color, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, religion, age, creed, ancestry, veteran status, marital status, disability, or other classification protected by applicable law in the administration of any of its educational programs or activities or with respect to employment. E-Verify: Ursinus College participates in the federal E-Verify program to confirm the identity and employment authorization of all newly hired employees. Employment is contingent upon completion of the Form I-9 and verification through E-Verify. This position may be offered at a different title or level, depending on the background, qualifications, and experience of the candidate selected. @ursinuscollege Powered by Curator.io Campus Map Webmail Library Editor Login Offices and Services Employment Contact Us Berman Museum Title IX and Sex Discrimination Campus Store & Books Web Accessibility Calendars Operating Hours and Service Updates Facebook X / Twitter Instagram YouTube ©\n            2026 Ursinus College. All rights reserved."
    },
    "http://www.hercjobs.org": {
      "title": "ENRICH MINDS AND SHAPE FUTURES. EXPLORE HIGHER ED JOBS.",
      "description": "Higher Ed Jobs - Higher Education Recruitment Consortium JOB SEEKER LOGIN HERCONNECT (MEMBER LOGIN) Menu Job Seeker Resources Search Jobs Create an Account Career Advice Ebooks Virtual Career Fairs Podcasts Webinars Dual Careers Resources Specialized Career Hubs Employer Resources Become a Member Products and Rates Post a Job Regional HERCs Toolkits About Us Menu Job Seeker Resources Search Jobs Create an Account Career Advice Ebooks Virtual Career Fairs Podcasts Webinars Dual Careers Resources Specialized Career Hubs Employer Resources Become a Member Products and Rates Post a Job Regional HERCs Toolkits About Us ENRICH MINDS AND SHAPE FUTURES. EXPLORE HIGHER ED JOBS. All States Alabama Alaska Arizona Arkansas California Colorado Connecticut D.C. Delaware Florida Georgia Hawaii Idaho Illinois Indiana Iowa Kansas Kentucky Louisiana Maine Maryland Massachusetts Michigan Minnesota Mississippi Missouri Montana Nationwide Nebraska Nevada New Hampshire New Jersey New Mexico New York North Carolina North Dakota Ohio Oklahoma Oregon Pennsylvania Rhode Island South Carolina South Dakota Tennessee Texas Utah Vermont Virginia Washington West Virginia Wisconsin Wyoming Canada International All Job Types Academic/Faculty Executive Staff/Administrative Dual Career Job Search Advanced Search All States Alabama Alaska Arizona Arkansas California Colorado Connecticut D.C. Delaware Florida Georgia Hawaii Idaho Illinois Indiana Iowa Kansas Kentucky Louisiana Maine Maryland Massachusetts Michigan Minnesota Mississippi Missouri Montana Nationwide Nebraska Nevada New Hampshire New Jersey New Mexico New York North Carolina North Dakota Ohio Oklahoma Oregon Pennsylvania Rhode Island South Carolina South Dakota Tennessee Texas Utah Vermont Virginia Washington West Virginia Wisconsin Wyoming Canada International All Job Types Academic/Faculty Executive Staff/Administrative Dual Career Job Search Advanced Search Help Make Higher Ed a Better Place to Work. Take Our Survey & Enter to Win Gift Cards. ARE YOU A JOB SEEKER? FIND YOUR IDEAL JOB IN HIGHER ED. Are you interested in starting or advancing your career in higher education? Create a free HERC Jobs account to: Search faculty, staff, and executive positions Set up custom job alerts to stay informed of new opportunities Create a profile and upload your resume/CV for increased visibility to recruiters Access free career resources, including articles, eBooks, and virtual career fairs CREATE AN ACCOUNT SEARCH JOBS ARE YOU AN EMPLOYER? EXPAND YOUR CANDIDATE POOL. Are you reaching qualified professionals? Do you have strategies for fostering a supportive workplace? Leverage HERC to: Connect with talented candidates on HERC Jobs, our job board and career resources website, through inclusive outreach methods Access tools, research, and a community of practice to reduce bias in your recruitment, selection, and retention efforts BECOME A MEMBER PRODUCTS & RATES Featured Articles Higher Ed Pulse Check: Making Higher Ed a Better Place to Work What would make higher education a better place to work? The group discusses the challenges and opportunities of stepping into... Read More Leading a Team With Neurodivergent Members Whether you are already leading or plan to lead an academic department, research lab, or administrative unit in higher education,... Read More Behind the Title: Alicia Simon, Dual Career Services Coordinator Alicia Simon, a dual career services professional, talks about the critical role dual career services play in faculty recruitment... Read More Load More Job Seeker Resources Career Advice Dual Career Resources eBooks Job Seeker Login Employer Resources Membership FAQs Toolkits Regional HERCs HERConnect Member Login HERC Member Institutions Full List of HERC Members Stay Connected with HERC Jobs Subscribe to our emails for updates on new resources and more! The Higher Education Recruitment Consortium (HERC) is a membership association dedicated to expanding the higher education candidate pool and fostering inclusive workplaces. HERC works to ensure member institutions – which include colleges, universities, hospitals, research labs, government agencies, and related organizations – are sites of belonging, where all faculty and staff can thrive. Through resources and collaboration, HERC supports member institutions in attracting and retaining top talent. For job seekers, HERC Jobs is a central hub for discovering, applying for, and succeeding in higher education careers. We believe an inclusive higher education workforce depends on systemic change best achieved through institutional collaboration, the development of innovative tools that can be shared and leveraged, and an engaged network of committed faculty and staff. Find it Fast Join HERC HERConnect (Member Login) Partners About Us Newsroom Contact Us Regional HERCS Carolinas Greater Chicago Midwest Metro New York & Southern Connecticut Michigan – Ohio – Western Pennsylvania – West Virginia Mid -Atlantic Midwest Mountain West New England New Jersey – Eastern Pennsylvania – Delaware Northern California Northwest Southeast South Midwest Southern California Upstate New York © 2000 – 2026 The Higher Education Recruitment Consortium is a project of the Tides Center, a 501(c)3 non-profit organization. Tides’ State Nonprofit Disclosures Sitemap | Terms | Privacy Policy Powered by WSI Digital Cookie settings Accept Cookies We use cookies so that we can remember you and understand how you use our site. If you do not agree with our use of cookies, please change the current settings found in our Cookie Policy . Otherwise, you agree to the use of the cookies as they are currently set.... Privacy & Cookies Policy Close Privacy Overview This website uses cookies to improve your experience while you navigate through the website. Out of these cookies, the cookies that are categorized as necessary are stored on your browser as they are essential for the working of basic functionalities of the website. We also use third-party cookies that help us analyze and understand how you use this website. These cookies will be stored in your browser only with your consent. You also have the option to opt-out of these cookies. But opting out of some of these cookies may have an effect on your browsing experience. Necessary Necessary Always Enabled Necessary cookies are absolutely essential for the website to function properly. This category only includes cookies that ensures basic functionalities and security features of the website. These cookies do not store any personal information. Non-necessary Non-necessary Any cookies that may not be particularly necessary for the website to function and is used specifically to collect user personal data via analytics, ads, other embedded contents are termed as non-necessary cookies. It is mandatory to procure user consent prior to running these cookies on your website. SAVE & ACCEPT"
